# Report how a task accepted by BeginTask ended. Served by syncai_robot_state
# on the relative name `end_task`, so it lands on <robot_id>/end_task
# (2026-11).
#
#   COMPLETED / CANCELED  the robot stops counting the task as running, and
#                         nothing else changes: a robot that was unconfirmed
#                         while it stood up is unconfirmed afterwards.
#   FAILED                the same, and ERROR is latched -- every later
#                         BeginTask is refused until an operator releases it
#                         with SetRobotState. `reason` is what the console
#                         shows meanwhile.
#
# Matched by task_id: a report for a task the robot is not running is a no-op
# answered success: false. That makes a repeated report harmless, and it means
# a syncai_robot_state restarted mid-task (UNINITIALIZED again, no task) does
# not latch ERROR from the run it forgot.

# 0 is deliberately no outcome, so a default-constructed request cannot
# report a completion nobody wrote -- RobotStatus's reasoning for
# UNINITIALIZED = 0. It is refused.
uint8 COMPLETED = 1
uint8 FAILED    = 2
uint8 CANCELED  = 3

# The id BeginTask was accepted with.
string task_id
uint8 outcome
# Why, for FAILED: one sentence an operator can read (the failed step's own
# error). Ignored for the other two.
string reason
---
bool success
string message
